# COLD WAR RENAISSANCE — CW-002H
## Dobrushin consensus × doubly-stochastic PFA undecidability
### The stationary-cutpoint singularity
Date: 2026-08-22
Status: EXACT THEOREM + 2025 COLLISION/COROLLARY

## 1. The apparent paradox

CW-002F showed that a finite family of strictly positive stochastic matrices is uniformly contractive in total variation.

Therefore all products forget their initial condition exponentially.

One might expect this to make threshold reachability easy.

A 2025 theorem of Günter Rote shows the opposite.

There exist PFAs with:

- only \(7\) states;
- \(4\) strictly positive doubly-stochastic transition matrices;
- a single accepting state;
- cutpoint
  \[
  \lambda=\frac17;
  \]

for which emptiness is undecidable.

An even stronger version fixes six positive doubly-stochastic transition matrices and leaves only the starting distribution as variable input.

Thus:

\[
\boxed{
\text{uniform exponential mixing does not imply decidable transient threshold reachability}.
}
\]

The reason is a knife-edge threshold at the common stationary value.

