## 2. General common-stationary margin theorem

Let

\[
\Sigma=\{P_a:a\in A\}
\]

be a finite family of rational stochastic matrices.

Assume:

1. all generators share a common invariant distribution \(\nu\):
   \[
   \nu P_a=\nu;
   \]
2. they are uniformly Dobrushin-contracting:
   \[
   \rho:=\max_a\delta(P_a)<1.
   \]

Let \(\mu\) be an initial distribution and let \(f\) be a bounded reward/output vector.

For a word \(w\) of length \(k\),

\[
|\mu P_wf-\nu f|
\le
\operatorname{osc}(f)
TV(\mu P_w,\nu),
\]

where

\[
\operatorname{osc}(f)
=
\max_i f_i-\min_i f_i.
\]

By contraction,

\[
TV(\mu P_w,\nu)
\le
\rho^kTV(\mu,\nu).
\]

Therefore:

### Theorem CW-002H.1 — Uniform stationary-envelope law

\[
\boxed{
|\mu P_wf-\nu f|
\le
\operatorname{osc}(f)
\rho^{|w|}
TV(\mu,\nu)
\qquad
\forall w.
}
\]

This is uniform over every switching word.

